{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChAwN1jNfJSFdXHEY34Fm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run test:ts` pass; `go test ./...` still passes.\n\nTicket 03 is done. All 16 checklist items pass and everything is committed except `.redeye/notes.md`. Lint, typecheck and `npm run test:ts` (386 assertions) pass, and so does the full `npm test` (Go tests and launcher tests).\n\nWhat's in place for later tickets to import:\n\n1. **textsafe** (`src/textsafe/textsafe.ts`): `text`, `line`, `textBytes`, `lineBytes`. The byte versions check UTF-8 validity the way Go does and escape each bad byte separately. Lone surrogates become lowercase `\\uNNNN`.\n2. **gocompat strings** (`src/gocompat/strings.ts`): `isGoSpace`, `goTrimSpace`, `goExt`, `truncateUtf8`, `formatFixed2`, `compareBytes`, `goQuote`.\n3. **gocompat durations** (`src/gocompat/duration.ts`): `parseGoDuration` returns nanoseconds as a `bigint`, covering the full int64 range and its overflow errors. Also `isGoDuration`, `toMillis`, and `formatGoDuration`, which reproduces Go's `Duration.String`.\n4. **gocompat match** (`src/gocompat/match.ts`): `goPathMatch` is a direct port of Go `path.Match`. Any malformed pattern returns false.\n5. **fsutil** (`src/fsutil/atomic.ts`): `writeFileAtomic(target, body, opts)`. The options (`mode`, `tempPrefix`/`tempSuffix`, `dirMode`, `chmodDir`, `errorPrefix`) cover all three callers: trust, credentials and the gate. Without `errorPrefix`, each failure names its step, as the gate needs.\n6. **git** (`src/git/git.ts`): `git` (resolves a Buffer), `gitOk`, `gitRoot` and `GitError`. On abort the child gets SIGTERM, then SIGKILL after 1s. The call rejects with the abort reason only after the child has exited. It only reads `process.env` when the caller passes no `env`.\n7. **util** (`src/util/pool.ts`): `mapPool`. The first error or an abort stops new items from starting.\n\nThings worth knowing:\n\n- **The git runner's API differs from `spec/04-scope.md` 3.3.** I followed the ticket, which takes precedence. The function is named `git`, not `gitOut`. `env` replaces `process.env` instead of being merged over it, and a separate `extraEnv` is merged over `env`. The scope ticket should build on that.\n- **Testing the abort.** Each test puts a fake `git` script first on the `PATH` it passes in. The script records its pid, and the test checks that the process is gone after the call rejects. A second test makes the script ignore SIGTERM, so it covers the SIGKILL fallback; that one adds about a second to the run.\n- **Escapes in source get decoded.** My file-writing tool, and even quoted Bash heredocs, turned `\\uXXXX` escapes into the literal characters. I converted them back and checked that no non-ASCII is left in the source. I added a warning about this to `AGENTS.md`, along with the two lint rules I hit (`no-control-regex`, `no-labels`).\n- **Two commits failed lint.** My command chain committed before lint had passed, twice. The commit right after each one fixes it, and the final tree is clean.\n- **Red runs.** For each module, the failing run I saw was \"module not found\" before the implementation existed. I didn't see each assertion fail on its own first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":139052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":598},"output_tokens":876,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02187ea8-af9b-477f-868a-aa4728904d24","uuid":"a0f1d778-3510-4d29-9b5e-3e45c1305077","timestamp":"2026-11-18T19:22:45.841Z","request_id":"req_011ChAwN1XDyNKKso1Bq4Q9h"}
